WRAPPER NOTE (honesty): the web page is a THIN PROMOTION WRAPPER — it sets the page
title/subtitle (PageContainer title + subtitle) and embeds the shared <NotificationSettings />
component; it owns no data of its own (manifest: 0 data sources, 0 panels, 0 charts, 0 maps,
2 strings, requiredCount=2 — "renders from navigation args / local state"). The Android port is
faithful to that shape: BrowserNotificationsPage renders the title/subtitle header and composes
the PRE-EXISTING NotificationSettings feature view
(apps/android/app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/feature-views/NotificationSettings, package
io.teslasync.android.featureviews.notificationsettings) VERBATIM — the browser-permission action,
the per-event push toggles (alerts / export completions), the browser-tab-signal toggles, the
notification-sound master/per-channel/volume controls, and the full cache-then-network
loading/stale/error/content state matrix for the /settings document all come from that one shared
surface (DRY, ADR-006). It is NOT re-implemented or stubbed here (ADR-011).

PREDECESSOR NOTE (honesty): the NotificationSettings feature view (+ its ViewModel / Source / Model /
Glyphs and unit/UI tests), the S7 HttpSettingsRepository + S8 SettingsStore, and the device-local
WebPushPrefsStore / NotificationSoundPrefsStore / NotificationSoundPlayer seams already exist on this
branch (shared :core + :android compile green). The page binds the real shared holder end to end via
notificationSettingsSource(HttpSettingsRepository(container.api, container.cacheStore),
SharedPreferencesWebPushPrefsStore(context), SharedPreferencesNotificationSoundPrefsStore(context),
ToneGeneratorNotificationSoundPlayer()); the page-local repository mirrors the GlanceRoute precedent
(build a page-local store over the shared resilient client + offline cache the container exposes). No
predecessor was stubbed or bypassed.

NAV NOTE: the `notificationsBrowser` -> /notifications/browser destination already exists in
Destinations.kt (pre-existing metadata row; RouteTableTest asserts "/notifications/browser" to
"notificationsBrowser"); this prompt only attaches host content via PageHosts.register, and the deep
