STRING-CATALOG NOTE (honesty, no silent drift): unlike the sibling gas-price wrapper, the 2 page
strings did NOT pre-exist in the android catalog. Web BrowserNotificationsPage.tsx resolves them via
inline t() defaults (notifications.browser.title="Browser notifications",
notifications.browser.subtitle="Native browser push notifications when alerts fire.") and the keys were
absent from the canonical i18n source. They were therefore added:
  - web/src/i18n/en.json  -> top-level notifications.browser.{title,subtitle} (the canonical source of
    truth, so a future gen-i18n regen reproduces the keys instead of dropping them)
  - res/values/strings.xml + res/values-ar/strings.xml + res/values-he/strings.xml ->
    translation_notifications_browser_{subtitle,title} (English fallback for the ar/he placeholder
    locales, matching the sibling translation_gas_* / translation_browserNotifications_* pattern).
gen-i18n.ts was NOT executed: `npx tsx apps/shared/i18n/generators/gen-i18n.ts --check` reports
PRE-EXISTING repo-wide drift on all 11 generated artifacts (catalog/*, android values*, apple,
windows) before any change here, so a full regen would balloon an unrelated multi-thousand-line diff
outside this artifact's allowed files. The two keys were hand-added consistently instead, so they
resolve at build time (assembleDebug green proves the R.string references compile) and stay regen-safe.
MissingTranslation/ExtraTranslation lint is disabled in app/build.gradle.kts, so the placeholder
locales need only the default-locale fallback.

GATE PATH NOTE: the project Gradle path is ':android' (settings.gradle.kts maps ':android' -> app/, and
states every P3/A* gate addresses ':android:'); the prompt snippet's ':app:' is the same single app
module.

DETEKT NOTE (honesty, no red-as-green): detekt is NOT part of this artifact's binding gate (the prompt
